	:url-ApplePodcasts "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/computer-minds-mike-levin-panpsychism/id6793816529?i=1000784637094"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """In this episode of Philosophy, Programs, and Prompts, Casey Hart (@OntologyExplained) and Carl Brown(@InternetOfBugs) dive deep into biologist Michael Levin’s provocative claims about cognition in basic computer algorithms. Does a distributed bubble sort display \"delayed gratification\" or proto-cognitive desires? Or are these emergent properties simply artifacts of velocity differences, ill-defined terms, and after-the-fact p-hacking?

Casey and Carl break down the computer science, philosophical frameworks (substrate independence, Platonic spaces, and supervenience), and the importance of rigorous, falsifiable hypothesis testing when crossing disciplinary boundaries.""" ;
